      "writtenOn": "2025-08-28T17:41:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to confirm, there\u0027s no query behavioral impact from this, only a \"cosmetic\" difference in which prefix string (\"is\" or \"status\") would be returned?\n\nI\u0027m not claiming that difference isn\u0027t important, just trying to see if this matters enough to be backported. I think the only significant, stable branch, non-plugin use of that predicate string would be in ApprovalCopier. It might be confusing for a user to see a different prefix there, but it\u0027s also very unlikely someone is using a status predicate in approval copy conditions.",
      "revId": "1b4cb7b7ad97527a21d62c0c5f00bc42a2b8bc48",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52bf1633_488c4a92",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-29T06:52:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it\u0027s probably not important enough to be back-ported.\n\nFor submit-requirement this is only theoretically relevant because there is no use-case to use is:open/status:open in a submit requirement expression. But if there was it could happen that the submit requirement expression contains \"is:open\" and then we would return \"status:open\" as a passing/failing atom. In this case the UI couldn\u0027t underline \"is:open\" with green/red to show the user that this atom is passing/failing.",
      "parentUuid": "7faf4092_76f4f12b",
      "revId": "1b4cb7b7ad97527a21d62c0c5f00bc42a2b8bc48",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
  ],
